{
    "$comment": [
        "BASELINE OF KNOWN, UNFIXED VIOLATIONS — NOT AN EXCLUSION LIST.",
        "",
        "The engine imported in E1 violates the purity invariant in the fourteen places catalogued",
        "in docs/adr/0001-upstream-purity-audit.md. E2 fixes them one at a time. Until then the",
        "harness would be red on every PR, which trains everyone to ignore it.",
        "",
        "So the suite asserts the violation set EQUALS this baseline, exactly:",
        "  - a NEW violation fails the build (a regression)",
        "  - a violation that DISAPPEARS also fails the build, telling you to tighten this file",
        "",
        "That second half is what makes this a ratchet rather than a mute button. Entries may only",
        "ever be REMOVED, and removing one means the corresponding ADR 0001 site is fixed. Adding",
        "an entry to make CI green is the thing CLAUDE.md forbids.",
        "",
        "Mapping to ADR 0001:",
        "  attribute style / data-darkreader-inline-*  -> items 1-3, 5, 6 (P0/P1, the Sheets failure)",
        "  data-darkreader-mode / -scheme on <html>    -> item 7",
        "  data-darkreader-proxy-injected on <html>    -> item 9",
        "  added <meta> under <head>                   -> item 10 (transient; only the observer sees it)",
        "  #text churn under pre#serialized            -> the editor serializing our write into its own model",
        ""
    ],
